<p><b>Document Coverage</b> shows the selected LiveDocs of the current project as a graph. Two documents are connected when work items of one are linked to work items of the other with one of the selected link roles (1 to 5, e.g. <code>satisfies</code>).</p>
<ul>
  <li>The <b>upstream</b> document holds the link targets (e.g. a customer specification) and is drawn on the left. The arrow follows the link, from the <b>downstream</b> document to the upstream one.</li>
  <li>Each line shows the role names and the number of links. The details give the downstream items with links and the upstream items covered.</li>
  <li>Each upstream document shows its <b>coverage</b>: share of its work items with at least one link from a shown downstream document. Click it for the uncovered items.</li>
</ul>
<p>No document selected means all documents of the project. Work items of the excluded types (default <code>heading</code>) are not counted. Links inside one document are ignored. In PDF export, the widget renders a static graph and the coverage tables.</p>
